^"stream"{
 >>[2026-10-28 18:27] plan — the creator told factshift's origin: a better Wikipedia, until it was clear that improving on it would take knowing how people learn. Spw grew from that, to represent information with many dimensions from many perspectives (ecestudent@ece.120~?[transistors work.how]). factshift.center is new this year, extending the concept into a more experimental domain. The factshift.com domain page now tells that, uncommitted. This plan proposes a neuroplasticity topic as the same question asked of the learner: four ideas, each with one figure and one thing to try on factshift.center's canvas. Its claims are listed with sources to check, and nothing is built.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:48] probe — wonder_neuroplasticity_home, read from the hubs as they stand. Pedagogy already carries retrieval and spacing: "Revisit through retrieval" in #pedagogy-habits, a Retrieval Practice card, and The Science of Learning (#learning-science-bridge). Andragogy carries adult principles (#andragogy-principles) and no memory content; biochemistry has none. A reader with a question about relearning would meet pedagogy first. The ~#expect, andragogy, holds on the topic's reason but not on what a reader finds now. Left for the creator.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:52] revise — "Two learners, one claim" does not run on the canvas as it is. ?spw= holds one line (holdSpwLineFromAddress in the app's src/js/init/root.ts), and compoundOf in line-anatomy.ts groups a chain to the left, so two lines joined by a mark would split on the second learner's own ~. PLAN.md now names the second line as new mechanics. Also added: a guard against clinical or diagnostic framing (no conditions, no therapy claims), one-session slices, and a proposal that Fire together show its state in the held line, {a, b} turning to {a.b}, with its limit said.
}

^"cache"{
